---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PARTS, PEERS } from "../data/landscape.js";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <header class="top">
    <span class="top-meta">lifeos research · v0</span>
    <a class="top-link" href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness"
      >github</a
    >
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1 class="brand">meta-harness</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The coding agent is the employee. Something else has to be the shop —
        or you are.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="scene" aria-labelledby="scene-title">
      <h2 id="scene-title" class="sr">A Tuesday</h2>
      <p>
        You ask Claude Code to cancel an order. It needs the API, the web app,
        and a design-system dialog. Three repos. You clone, branch, paste
        context, babysit PRs so they land together.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last week you already decided retries belong in the gateway — in a chat
        that no longer exists. Git has the diff. Nobody has the why. Your
        other laptop ran the same dead end yesterday.
      </p>
      <p class="punch">
        That gap — not “better prompts” — is what this notebook is about.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bundle" aria-labelledby="bundle-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="bundle-title">The bundle</h2>
        <p>
          Not one product shape. Organs. Peers ship different subsets hard.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="matrix">
        {
          PARTS.map((part) => (
            <li>
              <span class="matrix-id">{part.label}</span>
              <span class="matrix-blurb">{part.blurb}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="field" aria-labelledby="field-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="field-title">Who owns what</h2>
        <p>Center of gravity — not a feature scorecard.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="owners">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Name</th>
            <th scope="col">Owns hard</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            PEERS.map((p) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">
                  {p.url ? (
                    <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                      {p.name}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    p.name
                  )}
                </th>
                <td>{p.owns}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">
        <mark>Cerebras Knowledge</mark> is retrieve, done well. It can live
        inside a fuller stack. It is not continuity + scope + constraint by
        itself — same as a tracker that only does work, or a sandbox that only
        does constraint.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="lifeos" aria-labelledby="lifeos-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="lifeos-title">LifeOS cut</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/personal-ai-os">personal-ai-os</a>
          — what we actually run.
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre class="cut" aria-label="LifeOS cut of the bundle"><code>world model     folio · ledger · trackers          ← meaning
walker          PersonalOS OPEVL                    ← phases
work / run / session                                ← coordination
muscle          Fly Deep Agents · opt. Claude/Codex ← harness

heavy:  meaning · walker · work
thin:   cross-repo scope · session handoff · OS sandbox
open:   which thin gap becomes the product</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="open" aria-labelledby="open-title">
      <h2 id="open-title">Open</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Which organs stay thin forever in LifeOS?</li>
        <li>Is the asset the wrap, or the world model that dispatches wraps?</li>
        <li>Handoff, sandbox, or cross-repo — what forces the next bet?</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="foot">
    <p>
      Written beside LifeOS. Labels move. MIT ·
      <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/meta-harness">source</a>
    </p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
